@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: a provider key in the workspace .env — which backend READS it, which merely lets it be read, and the wrong mechanism in the warning about it
' session: 6769e470-377b-4b51-98c8-a84637f468f7
' PLANNED — nothing here is implemented; _spec/_plans/ is exempt from the SPEC-reference rule.
'   the warning itself ........... internal/credentials/credentials.go (WarnMountedSecrets)
'   the prelude it blames ........ packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh (load_env)
'   the mask it credits .......... internal/workspace/mount.go (isolateEnv, maskEnvMounts)
'   the sbx startup command ...... internal/backend/sandbox/sandbox.go (Setup.Startup)
'   where a key SHOULD rest ...... _spec/_plans/secret-custody.puml
'   the sbx credential path ...... _spec/internal/sbx/credential-path.puml
'   what the agent may hold ...... _spec/_paradigms/credential-boundary.puml
'   the tiers that mask .......... _spec/internal/egress/egress-tiers.puml
'   why clone mode has tracked-only files _spec/internal/sbx/clone-workspace.puml
'
'   THE CLASS THIS IS AN INSTANCE OF: _spec/_paradigms/workspace-boundary.puml
'     — direct mode imports the host's file semantics; a clone re-materialises
'     them. Presence, mode/ownership, architecture and which-tree are one cause
'     meeting four properties of a file. Keep only this file's distinct half.
'
' ── THE WARNING, AND THE ONE CLAIM IN IT THAT DOES NOT HOLD ────────────────
' On every sbx run whose workspace holds a `.env` and whose environment holds a
' provider key, proveo says:
'
'   "<dir>/.env is inside the sandbox workspace and holds a provider key — the
'    agent's prelude sources it with `set -a`, so the key becomes agent
'    environment whatever egress tier you picked"
'
' The conclusion is right and the mechanism is wrong. On sbx the prelude never
' runs: `sbx run` does not execute the image ENTRYPOINT, the Kit's only startup
' command is `proveo-seed`, and `proveo_seed` calls ten helpers —
' proveo_sync_state, render_subagents, accept_workspace_trust,
' proveo_provision_toolchain, proveo_enable_claude_lsp_plugins,
' proveo_compose_house_rules, proveo_apply_ui_defaults,
' proveo_install_claude_hooks, proveo_seed_browser_skills, proveo_chrome_bridge
' — and `load_env` is not among them. The only thing proveo writes into the
' sandbox's `.bashrc` is _proveo_persist_tool_env's block: PATH, GOROOT, GOPATH,
' VIRTUAL_ENV. Nothing there sources a dotenv.
'
' Two comments in this tree disagree about it, which is how the defect survived:
'
'   credentials.go     "with no PROVEO_EGRESS_MODE in the Kit the in-container
'                       prelude SOURCES the .env with `set -a`"
'   entrypoint-lib.sh  "sbx never runs the image entrypoint and the seed is its
'                       startup command"
'
' Only one of those can be true, and the second is the one the code shows.
'
' What IS true on sbx is plainer and no smaller: the workspace is mounted WHOLE
' at its own host path, nothing masks `.env*` there, so the file sits in the
' agent's cwd and `cat .env` reads the key. That distinction is not cosmetic — a
' wrong mechanism names a wrong fix. "The prelude sources it" invites putting
' PROVEO_EGRESS_MODE into the Kit's environment block, which would change
' nothing whatsoever, because no prelude reads it on that backend.
'
' ── CORRECTION 2026-09-09: THE PRELUDE DOES RUN NOW (measured) ─────────────
' The section above is true of the MIXIN era and false of the path proveo takes
' today. `kind: sandbox` declares the image ENTRYPOINT itself —
' `kit.Sandbox.Entrypoint = imageEntrypoint(in)` — and the rendered Kit carries
'     sandbox:
'       entrypoint: [dumb-init, --, cecli-entrypoint]
' so sbx execs it. Read from a live sandbox's own process table:
'     pid 556  dumb-init -- cecli-entrypoint
'     pid 557  /opt/cecli/bin/python3 /opt/cecli/bin/cecli --rules …
'
' A SECOND, INDEPENDENT PROOF, because a process name could be argued with.
' pid 557 holds GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY=proxy-managed. The Kit declares
' four credentials (ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, GEMINI_API_KEY, OPENAI_API_KEY,
' XAI_API_KEY) and that name is not among them. Only the Google bridge creates
' it — `load_env` itself, and BridgeGoogleKeys in proveo-entrypoint. So the
' prelude ran, and it ran far enough to reach the bridge that sits AFTER the
' `.env` source.
'
' WHICH REVERSES THIS PLAN'S VERDICT ON THE REPAIR. "Putting
' PROVEO_EGRESS_MODE into the Kit's environment block would change nothing
' whatsoever" was correct when nothing read it; on the sandbox-kind path
' `load_env` reads it on line 88 and takes the skip branch. The Kit already has
' an `environment.variables` map — it carries MCP_GATEWAY_URL — so this is a
' one-entry change, not a new mechanism.
'
' The tier vocabulary is deliberately inert on sbx (policy-baseline.puml), so
' spelling it `PROVEO_EGRESS_MODE=allowlist` there smuggles a value that means
' nothing on that backend. A purpose-named flag reads honestly and needs adding
' to internal/contract/egress_vocabulary_test.go, which pins the vocabulary.
'
' ── AND IT DID NOT MATTER ON THAT RUN, FOR THE REASON THIS PLAN PREDICTED ──
' `load_env` took the NON-skip branch, looked for a `.env`, and XAI_API_KEY was
' still `proxy-managed` in the agent afterwards. So nothing was sourced over the
' sentinel — because the run was a CLONE, and a clone carries tracked files
' only. The CLONE note below called this exactly right; it is now measured
' rather than reasoned.
'
' So the exposure that remains is this plan's other half, unchanged and still
' correct: OFF clone mode the workspace is mounted whole and `cat .env` reads
' the key. Two independent closes now exist for two different postures, and
' neither covers the other.
'
' The incident that produced these measurements was NOT this defect — it was xAI
' answering 403 for an account out of credits, with a stale host-wide secret
' deciding which account. See _spec/internal/sbx/kit-sandbox-credential-gap.puml
' and _spec/_plans/host-held-provider-keys.puml.
'
' ── WHO ACTUALLY READS THE FILE ────────────────────────────────────────────
' Four postures, and only one of them sources anything:
'
'   docker · open|allowlist|review · brokered   `.env*` masked with /dev/null
'                                               (isolateEnv), AND load_env takes
'                                               its skip branch. Closed twice.
'   docker · any tier · --credentials forward   isolateEnv returns false, so the
'                                               real file is mounted; load_env
'                                               still skips on those three tiers.
'                                               READABLE, not sourced.
'   docker · firewall (or any other tier)       no mask, no skip: load_env sources
'                                               it with `set -a`. This is the only
'                                               posture the warning describes.
'   sbx · every tier                            mounted whole, unmasked, no
'                                               prelude at all. READABLE.
'
' So the sentence proveo prints on sbx describes the one case that is not sbx.
title PLANNED — a key in the workspace .env: sourced on one posture, readable on most

component "**""<ws>/.env""**\na provider key at rest beside the code" as ENVF <<error>>
component "the warning\nright conclusion, wrong mechanism" as WARN <<error>>

node "docker + egress" as DOCKER <<host>> {
  component """maskEnvMounts""\n/dev/null over every ""\.env*""" as MASK <<app>>
  component """load_env""\n""set -a"", skipped on three tiers" as PRE <<app>>
}

node "sbx" as SBXN <<host>> {
  component "the workspace, mounted WHOLE\nat its own host path — no mask exists" as WS <<error>>
  component "no prelude runs here\nno ENTRYPOINT; startup is ""proveo-seed""" as NOPRE <<app>>
}

component """--clone""\ncarries TRACKED files only" as CLONE <<app>>
component """secretref"" -> ""sbx secret set""\nthe key never enters the repo" as STORE <<app>>
component "the agent" as AGENT <<app>>

ENVF ARROW_MAIN MASK
ENVF ARROW_MAIN PRE
ENVF ARROW_MAIN WS
MASK ARROW_ERROR AGENT : nothing left to read
PRE ARROW_QUEUE AGENT : sourced only off the masking tiers
WS ARROW_ERROR AGENT : ""cat .env"" — the whole exposure
NOPRE ARROW_ERROR WARN : the claim that does not hold
CLONE ARROW_MAIN WS : a gitignored ""\.env"" never arrives
STORE ARROW_MAIN AGENT : injected, never mounted

note bottom of WARN
  **Right conclusion, wrong mechanism.** The key
  IS reachable on sbx — because the file is
  mounted and unmasked, not because anything
  sources it. The difference is the fix.
end note

note top of WARN
  **The repair works now.** This note used to
  call ""PROVEO_EGRESS_MODE"" in the Kit a no-op.
  On the sandbox-kind path ""load_env"" reads it
  and skips — so the mechanism was wrong for a
  while, and then the code changed under it.
end note

note bottom of PRE
  **""set -a"" is the docker story, and not all of
  it.** Sourcing is skipped on open, allowlist
  and review, so it happens only on the tiers
  that do not mask — firewall and below.
end note

note bottom of MASK
  **Masking is credential-gated, not just
  tier-gated.** ""isolateEnv"" is false under
  ""--credentials forward"", so that posture
  mounts the real file on every tier.
end note

note bottom of WS
  **There is no per-file overlay to hang a mask
  on.** sbx takes DIRECTORY workspaces at their
  own host paths, so ""\.env"" arrives with
  everything else or not at all.
end note

note top of WS
  **And deleting it inside is not an option.**
  The mount is the operator's own directory over
  virtiofs, so a shred in the sandbox shreds
  their file. The answer has to be upstream.
end note

note bottom of NOPRE
  **Superseded 2026-09-09.** True of the mixin;
  ""kind: sandbox"" declares the ENTRYPOINT, and a
  live process table shows ""cecli-entrypoint""
  running. The prelude DOES run — see the
  correction block above.
end note

note top of NOPRE
  **The rc block carries no secret either.**
  ""_proveo_persist_tool_env"" puts PATH, GOROOT,
  GOPATH and VIRTUAL_ENV in ""\.bashrc"" — a
  toolchain, not an environment file.
end note

note bottom of CLONE
  **The default posture already closes it.** A
  clone carries TRACKED files only, and a
  ""\.env"" is gitignored by habit, so it never
  reaches the sandbox at all.
end note

note top of CLONE
  **A default is not a guarantee.**
  ""--clone=false"", a sub-scope, a non-repo and a
  linked worktree each fall back to the mounted
  tree — and a COMMITTED ""\.env"" clones fine.
end note

note bottom of STORE
  **The only close that empties the file.**
  ""keychain:"" resolves host-side and
  ""sbx secret set"" hands the value in on stdin,
  so no key is left in the repo to read.
end note

note bottom of ENVF
  **The file is itself a posture.** A plaintext
  key beside the code is what secret-custody
  calls exposure (a); this plan is only about
  who can READ it once a run starts.
end note

legend bottom
  **The order to do it in — the first step is a sentence**
  ==
  **1. Say what is true on sbx.** Two things are, and they close different
  postures: OFF a clone the file is mounted and readable; ON any posture the
  prelude now runs, so a Kit flag can stop it being sourced.
  --
  **2. Pin which comment is right — and it is the one this plan doubted.**
  ""WarnMountedSecrets"" said the prelude sources the file; that is now measured
  true on the sandbox-kind path. A contract test over the Kit's ENTRYPOINT, not
  just its startup command, is what would have kept this straight.
  --
  **3. Name the two escapes where the problem is read.** ""--clone"" keeps a
  gitignored ""\.env"" out of the sandbox entirely, and a ""keychain:"" reference keeps
  the key out of the file. Neither appears in the warning today.
  --
  **4. Then decide whether sbx warns or refuses.** It cannot mask a file inside a
  directory mount, so the candidates are: warn harder, refuse the run, or make the
  host store the documented default and leave the warning as the nudge toward it.
  ==
  **Left open on purpose.** Whether a COMMITTED ""\.env"" should block an sbx run
  outright; whether the docker mask should key on ""--credentials forward"" rather
  than on the tier; and whether ""load_env"" should stop sourcing dotenvs at all now
  that a broker and a host store both exist.
end legend
@enduml
